trial or experiment.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The weight, measured in grams, of sugar in a bowl” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262584 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105860 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ee39554-fd77-5e90-baa8-f9320ffc3398" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Continuous Random Variables Given in Context" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049638 :topic/id #uuid "0748b9c2-fae7-5522-9655-db9e6f1d50c0" :topic/math-academy-id 1347 :topic/title "Probability Density Functions of Continuous Random Variables"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03b50dba-8694-51ea-a35e-b4bd86bec3d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463562} {:answer/id #uuid "900c7459-17eb-5177-a271-c7469575a0f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "900c7459-17eb-5177-a271-c7469575a0f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463563} :answer-field/id #uuid "6731853f-5334-5c22-a346-9409f0a2a22e" :answer-field/key "The percentage of impurity in a batch of chemicals" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464715} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00fc378b-457d-547f-8b99-28a3ad28bcbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463564} {:answer/id #uuid "13962be2-385c-5e4a-bc9f-42b3b58c82c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00fc378b-457d-547f-8b99-28a3ad28bcbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463564} :answer-field/id #uuid "177bd183-0ce9-5f65-af93-708eccfacd23" :answer-field/key "The area of an equilateral triangle with a side of $2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464716} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f330944-206b-5ef2-ad02-310197bb5eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463566} {:answer/id #uuid "0e9ccba2-8e0b-5551-afcb-5e2c8f4fcf16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e9ccba2-8e0b-5551-afcb-5e2c8f4fcf16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463567} :answer-field/id #uuid "5890b149-b511-5044-bed9-09b94810af9d" :answer-field/key "The amount of snowfall, in centimeters, in a randomly selected city in January 2022" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ec51dd0-d568-5d90-9c62-e7294f84d1e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-126061" :question/problem "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/05/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The percentage of impurity in a batch of chemicals”  describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $[0,100]$ (since the percentage can be anywhere between $0%$ and $100%$).\n\n- Statement “The area of an equilateral triangle with a side of $2$” does *not* describe a continuous random variable. The area of an equilateral triangle with a given side length is not the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\n- Statement “The amount of snowfall, in centimeters, in a randomly selected city in January 2022” describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $[0,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The percentage of impurity in a batch of chemicals”; “The amount of snowfall, in centimeters, in a randomly selected city in January 2022” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262585 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050432 :topic/id #uuid "48930849-af42-52a8-8e89-28eb54e1d4a5" :topic/math-academy-id 49 :topic/title "The Cartesian Product"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f6dace5-df44-51df-b091-e335e6a5f910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448248} {:answer/id #uuid "a0c8cb0a-553c-5b2b-9c44-e2a274e9c8da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0c8cb0a-553c-5b2b-9c44-e2a274e9c8da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448249} :answer-field/id #uuid "06b3