r/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463674} {:answer/id #uuid "1cd0c675-2a7c-531b-87e6-0dd86ba970a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e9af7d3-2561-554a-ab5b-17fb671ab226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463674} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b205a91-05e2-588d-9438-a4d81472431f" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7075e5f8-1ac7-5f5f-9b8e-5fb44e2f53d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-128152" :question/problem "Which of the following completes the statement so that it is true:\n\n*If a $2\\times 2$-matrix $A$ is invertible, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ . *\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\nNow, since the first part of the invertible matrix theorem is true ($A$ is invertible), all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem, only options “$Ax=0$ has exactly one solution” and “The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point” give us true statements: \n\n- *If $A$ is invertible, then $Ax=0$ has exactly one solution.* $\\,✓$\n\n- *If $A$ is invertible, then The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.* $\\,✓$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262906 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048146 :topic/id #uuid "832923c0-f0e3-599f-af85-37cb7dae2658" :topic/math-academy-id 153 :topic/title "The Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "938435d8-69e4-5177-83be-c2661b220df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437788} {:answer/id #uuid "b0acf52f-1926-563b-90fe-5bd5c838a2cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "938435d8-69e4-5177-83be-c2661b220df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437788} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef069a99-e51d-5c41-b3dd-fbe618b3ae29" :answer-field/key "$det(Q)=-5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438923} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fda1810e-40d9-5b5a-8ed9-7de0e91b6696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437790} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8badb5-ccf3-54b7-bf14-15f19c3c783e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fda1810e-40d9-5b5a-8ed9-7de0e91b6696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437790} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6baa2c-bfa2-5841-829c-446168fc4d31" :answer-field/key "$det(Q)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438924} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd3030ea-f56b-54f2-b19e-0fe96063ba8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437792} {:answer/id #uuid "13768b60-6037-5979-87a7-85e46aa637f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd3030ea-f56b-54f2-b19e-0fe96063ba8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437792} :answer-field/id #uuid "10609156-1bc3-5176-82f7-7da72d8cac5c" :answer-field/key "$Q$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f86fe2f1-042a-5183-8a18-518a658cc1a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-128474" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $Q$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(9-5)-1(6-3)-1(10-9) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4-3-1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, none of the statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262908 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048146 :topic/id #uuid "832923c0-f0e3-599f-af85-37cb7dae2658" :topic/math-academy-id 153 :topic/title "The Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9c8a655-dc30-5747-b5e0-efd4fa464943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437794} {:answer/id #uuid "b3238a25-1600-54c9-a92e-d6b1f31166ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9c8a655-dc30-5747-b5e0-efd4fa464943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437794} :answer-field/id #uuid "0457a549-1799-5124-a11e-6cbe8bf02f40" :answer-field/key "$T$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438926} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86770289-d595-5a74-8241-7f7eaf943501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437796} {:answer/id #uuid "0065df67-0fde-5ae4-ab1b-04075255afaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0065df67-0fde-5ae4-ab1b-04075255afaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437797} :answer-field/id #uuid "48c446f0-c232-5d1a-a9fa-08c4d973bbe4" :answer-field/key "$T$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438927} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d221ff-7342-5189-8083-2e45e2305d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437798} {:answer/id #uuid "db168e14-a68a-5486-95d1-8d4686854e72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db168e14-a68a-5486-95d1-8d4686854e72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437799} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b5f6d45-4846-5d6c-b409-f20f073263eb" :answer-field/key "$det(T)=-30$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "898815e0-65a8-55f9-b81f-a64efbb5e7e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-128476" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1-3)-3(2-1)-5(6-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-2-3-25 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(T)=-30\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements “$T$ is **not** a singular matrix” and $det(T)=-30$ are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048146 :topic/id #uuid "832923c0-f0e3-599f-af85-37cb7dae2658" :topic/math-academy-id 153 :topic/title "The Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96a78a3a-a96f-5296-bb6f-17bd0c2c1029" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437812} {:answer/id #uuid "8a41bcde-2807-5a96-8245-df7493039a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a41bcde-2807-5a96-8245-df7493039a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437813} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d87a851-8d26-5425-83e8-dba94be07b21" :answer-field/key "$R$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438935} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d06dd62-d83d-54e9-b4ea-1974429d75ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437814} {:answer/id #uuid "423c9da1-fb5c-5eb1-aac0-e8f7d5033fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "423c9da1-fb5c-5eb1-aac0-e8f7d5033fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437815} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad0097cd-c1c7-5438-b4af-b5844d0cf50a" :answer-field/key "$det(R)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438936} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e2b6e65-193a-5e1a-ae4e-babcf8cd0b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437816} {:answer/id #uuid "4daf1704-b4bb-5190-aede-54368b9e49c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e2b6e65-193a-5e1a-ae4e-babcf8cd0b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437816} :answer-field/id #uuid "727b8a81-c497-5e39-8d74-82d5d2b34ab9" :answer-field/key "$det(R)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0d8a3d8-8c1e-55f4-b495-022734d0f802" :question/math-academy-id "q-128484" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $R$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{aligned}|-\\sqrt{2}|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(0+\\sqrt{2})-\\sqrt{2}(2+1)+2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3+2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(R)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements “$R$ is a singular matrix” and $det(R)=0$ are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262919 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8d807a6-7896-5045-a14a-908b58831340" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points Where a Gradient Vanishes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050143 :topic/id #uuid "3055ed78-44c0-5be7-9e08-cb26d881941a" :topic/math-academy-id 1934 :topic/title "The Gradient Vector"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fe7a32f-bd64-5c3a-ac51-aa8e847ab23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439495} {:answer/id #uuid "a5b19982-26ea-52cf-bfb6-891798ebe687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fe7a32f-bd64-5c3a-ac51-aa8e847ab23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439495} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c9b26fe-a648-553a-a416-e7a5675ab1fe" :answer-field/key "$(-1,0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8879c732-ca2d-5143-a4fe-4257993d10ca" :answer/type {