" :question/math-academy-id "q-129216" :question/problem "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x?$    \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous. \n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$  is closed, but the function is not defined at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4}]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4}].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $[-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4}]$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/title "Quiz 1" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045460 :db/ident :activity.type/assessment} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572821} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573363}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83ae652e-2ae3-5769-8809-9e4a8d2c09bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463706} {:answer/id #uuid "51c4eacd-7138-5c6a-b45b-debd2edc6b93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/val