2186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49e3d6a2-966f-5582-8eea-73e36881a138" :question/math-academy-id "q-129219" :question/problem "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)}?$ \n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $(-2,2]$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-2,4]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-2,4].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $(-2,4)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $[-2,4]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048980 :topic/id #uuid "d0f342d9-c70c-537f-9e04-f3b0beaf9c01" :topic/math-academy-id 2083 :topic/title "Row Echelon Form"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef8db13b-e915-5420-94d4-8b4458ce5fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463718} {:answer/id #uuid "fb7f11f5-58ab-59d2-afc1-9c23b39fc74e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb7f11f5-58ab-59d2-afc1-9c23b39fc74e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592