y "The planes are parallel." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449198} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a09c6d3-9e07-5bfa-a9af-913b460366de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448318} {:answer/id #uuid "401bbb80-3136-505b-91b2-a79e6cdcbae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "401bbb80-3136-505b-91b2-a79e6cdcbae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448319} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8a49394-7282-584c-b4ee-30af011d8280" :answer-field/key "The planes intersect on a line." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d967e86-9fda-51c5-b084-5eaf2a90df28" :question/math-academy-id "q-129239" :question/problem "Given the two planes $2x-5y+z+1=0$ and $3x-z+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $2x-5y+z+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,-5,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $3x-z+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,0,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$” is false. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨2,-5,1⟩\\times ⟨3,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =5i+5j+15k \\\\  & =⟨5,5,15⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The planes are parallel” is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050991 :topic/id #uuid "7789d7fa-bfec-58c3-afd1-afcff30a8748" :topic/math-academy-id 2539 :topic/title "The Intersection of Two Planes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff5f8263-677b-5643-9c09-fbb882cb5e5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448320} {:answer/id #uuid "7e00f930-9bc2-5a8f-b341-6b3bfb849414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e00f930-9bc2-5a8f-b341-6b3bfb849414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448321} :answer-field/id #uuid "c870b39a-efa3-5b75-abf3-729e6c1bb66c" :answer-field/key "The normal vectors of the planes are parallel." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449200} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddbba897-a72e-574e-bb64-100d9be232c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448322} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6d0ded-ecca-50de-8256-302276a8c0c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed6d0ded-ecca-50de-8256-302276a8c0c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448323} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d641374-fb2b-5515-9551-b1f94e91baca" :answer-field/key "The planes are parallel but not coincident." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449201} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4626da49-16af-5f92-be8b-0ede6458b582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448324} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ac4ea5-c3ac-52b8-b780-d761ee6ccd2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4626da49-16af-5f92-be8b-0ede6458b582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448324} :answer-field/id #uuid "7af67d6f-4108-5880-b4ff-5f30c21746cc" :answer-field/key "The planes are coincident." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48d9b691-f927-556a-a0f4-054f943d7dcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-129240" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x-y+2z=0$ and $9x-3y+6z+5=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x-y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,-1,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $9x-3y+6z+5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨9,-3,6⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement “The normal vectors of the planes are parallel” is true. Indeed, ${n}_{2}=3{n}_{1}.$ So, the normal vectors are parallel.\n\n- Statement “The planes are parallel but not coincident” is true, while statement “The planes are coincident” is false. \n\nFor the two planes to coincide, the equation of one plane should be a scalar multiple of the other. However, if we try to manipulate the equation of the second plane to resemble the equation of the first plane, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-3y+6z+5=0 \\\\ 3x-y+2z+\\frac{5}{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nClearly, this equation is not the same as the equation of the first plane. So, the planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statements “The normal vectors of the planes are parallel” and “The planes are parallel but not coincident” are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263001 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050991 :topic/id #uuid "7789d7fa-bfec-58c3-afd1-afcff30a8748" :topic/math-academy-id 2539 :topic/title "The Intersection of Two Planes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3bf1a8d-9dfc-5a03-8a7a-a12552a416b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448326} {:answer/id #uuid "30b819cc-54c9-5241-bcb2-0afe25ea1cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3bf1a8d-9dfc-5a03-8a7a-a12552a416b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448326} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9949ae3-b6d9-5ef1-8624-bc499988813e" :answer-field/key "The normal vectors of the planes are parallel." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449203} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f26368b7-3e6e-5297-9b4f-7695649ea137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448328} {:answer/id #uuid "d00fa2fb-b244-56ee-b0ac-1b84182ea9ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f26368b7-3e6e-5297-9b4f-7695649ea137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448328} :answer-field/id #uuid "c385d683-72a4-5ea4-b2a1-efdb9c6df55d" :answer-field/key "The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449204} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8b6f951-e1c6-5513-a35c-3fa485d07fab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448330} {:answer/id #uuid "8c5c44e0-de54-563d-a94e-0a2b9889f8e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c5c44e0-de54-563d-a94e-0a2b9889f8e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448331} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c21207d-f238-50e0-bf4e-370792bcf5f4" :answer-field/key "The planes intersect on a line." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c9f9477f-0f39-55d8-91e7-cff41b6de7c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-129241" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-3y+2z=0$ and $x-2y+5=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-3y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-3,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-2y+5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements “The normal vectors of the planes are parallel” and “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$” are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-2,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨4,2,1⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050991 :topic/id #uuid "7789d7fa-bfec-58c3-afd1-afcff30a8748" :topic/math-academy-id 2539 :topic/title "The Intersection of Two Planes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7823cc1d-e72d-50f4-af52-e5710e6619a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448332} {:answer/id #uuid "057d0176-e1f4-520c-a143-aa4e8964f2f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7823cc1d-e72d-50f4-af52-e5710e6619a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448332} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdffdf7c-e7ca-5a79-9cff-9ff74a794c8e" :answer-field/key "The normal vectors of the planes are parallel." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449206} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "555b8c2a-281e-59e0-989a-153d03514140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448334} {:answer/id #uuid "637cc037-e978-545a-891a-ad0bd8723150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555b8c2a-281e-59e0-989a-153d03514140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448334} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a72e661-92ba-514e-9b21-9c405c4b262e" :answer-field/key "The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449207} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030f35ea-269a-5b9f-b30e-0d3d46f40283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448336} {:answer/id #uuid "b29d3efe-e9d0-57f7-894c-28ab8000018d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b29d3efe-e9d0-57f7-894c-28ab8000018d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448337} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eee5865-067e-555f-8847-0162ac1e2d3e" :answer-field/key "The planes intersect on a line." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d75bf5e3-9255-56f7-a884-2df425d0b593" :question/math-academy-id "q-129258" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-5y+2z=0$ and $3x-2y+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-5y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-5,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $3x-2y+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements “The normal vectors of the planes are parallel” and “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$” are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-5,2⟩\\times ⟨3,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+6j+13k \\\\  & =⟨4,6,13⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050991 :topic/id #uuid "7789d7fa-bfec-58c3-afd1-afcff30a8748" :topic/math-academy-id 2539 :topic/title "The Intersection of Two Planes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b0007c9-b9d9-5073-9847-1328f8ba456f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448338} {:answer/id #uuid "c07d5de8-6189-5107-a5d0-b648d30f4e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b0007c9-b9d9-5073-9847-1328f8ba456f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448338} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c49eabf-4bf6-5c32-9685-79efc670c417" :answer-field/key "The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨7,15,2⟩.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449209} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14bb3934-f6ec-59cd-99ae-ebf070b84930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448340} {:answer/id #uuid "a7dc5079-c112-5095-af24-842397e211d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7dc5079-c112-5095-af24-842397e211d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448341} :answer-field/id #uuid "55c3de56-e97c-5d08-8dd0-16889f5908a4" :answer-field/key "The planes intersect on a line." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449210} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb8a1855-4689-53bf-ad30-730d170807be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448342} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4d1237-b5dc-5cb5-86d5-1b7a288207c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb8a1855-4689-53bf-ad30-730d170807be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448342} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dd284aa-2269-52c0-a105-e2d1597fba9e" :answer-field/key "The planes are coincident." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df6925db-161f-5f40-8f9d-0f308e52b4c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-129259" :question/problem "Given the two planes $2x-y+3z=0$ and $5x-2y+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $2x-y+3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,-1,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $5x-2y+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨5,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨7,15,2⟩.$” is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\times ⟨5,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =6i+15j+k \\\\  & =⟨6,15,1⟩\\ne ⟨7,15,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement “The planes are coincident” is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes cannot be coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050991 :topic/id #uuid "7789d7fa-bfec-58c3-afd1-afcff30a8748" :topic/math-academy-id 2539 :topic/title "The Intersection of Two Planes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "225965e7-ea8b-53cc-8c0e-59f84b35bad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448344} {:answer/id #uuid "44625f5b-937b-5938-b07c-f560e2643779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44625f5b-937b-5938-b07c-f560e2643779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448345} :answer-field/id #uuid "d07dfd5a-6ecb-5608-b7c1-bea7db6ba11f" :answer-field/key "The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨5,-13,1⟩.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f406006b-6b33-5be7-af63-0ad0b245352f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448346} {:answer/id #uuid "f15dcac9-93bd-55b2-9f31-b7ee83d2ce65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f406006b-6b33-5be7-af63-0ad0b245352f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448346} :answer-field/id #uuid "56b07353-6adf-5e95-9046-04d5131fb4b2" :answer-field/key "The planes are parallel." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d244ee5-d55d-5d5d-a779-19cd20f8d3e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448348} {:answer/id #uuid "81250b54-fda0-5220-8698-e14b62c96958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81250b54-fda0-5220-8698-e14b62c96958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448349} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f1dcfe-3ed7-5654-8b55-b7e27497c7e8" :answer-field/key "The planes intersect on a line." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "999cfdc7-ea79-5a7b-bd15-dce6f8b9e282" :question/math-academy-id "q-129260" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x+y-2z=0$ and $2x+y+3z+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x+y-2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+y+3z+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,1,3⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨5,-13,1⟩.$” is true. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,1,-2⟩\\times ⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =5i-13j+k \\\\  & =⟨5,-13,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The planes are parallel” is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the corresponding planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨5,-13,1⟩.$” and “The planes intersect on a line” only are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050991 :topic/id #uuid "7789d7fa-bfec-58c3-afd1-afcff30a8748" :topic/math-academy-id 2539 :topic/title "The Intersection of Two Planes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b9480da-b8d7-5635-acad-ba1da8240664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448350} {:answer/id #uuid "ac1933c0-bd2f-5aff-beae-cb8cda84293b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b9480da-b8d7-5635-acad-ba1da8240664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448350} :answer-field/id #uuid "f40e5e28-4f88-5130-b328-64606e612555" :answer-field/key "The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨-3,12,6⟩.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449215} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b291afa3-882c-5323-96b3-be71495fa5ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448352} {:answer/id #uuid "c25385b7-80d0-51da-88a9-662a5e5b2c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c25385b7-80d0-51da-88a9-662a5e5b2c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448353} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a4987ef-c77c-5b41-994f-27c06e153327" :answer-field/key "The planes intersect on a line." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449216} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a59e55b-0aa1-51df-b3d5-69f5f25a9700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448354} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf7ba73-0774-51da-bccc-e7f1bc26d6dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a59e55b-0aa1-51df-b3d5-69f5f25a9700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448354} :answer-field/id #uuid "71c03d44-f207-5cb2-b332-ad7675261ad8" :answer-field/key "The planes are coincident." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d9644136-e70e-5412-95e4-ddf24de80c84" :question/math-academy-id "q-129261" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-y+2z=0$ and $5x+y-13=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $5x+y-13=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨5,1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨-3,12,6⟩.$” is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-1,2⟩\\times ⟨5,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-2i+10j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,10,6⟩\\ne ⟨-3,12,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the corresponding planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement “The planes are coincident” is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes could not be coincident either.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29610715-333d-5e0c-9328-eec1d45f56ed" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Limits Along Different Paths for Multivariable Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048449 :topic/id #uuid "a05758d1-f2b4-5a86-b7b0-c2a4bb6dcb85" :topic/math-academy-id 1931 :topic/title "Limits and Continuity of Multivariable Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c16c662e-6c36-5bf3-9a52-d68e7902ba15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463760} {:answer/id #uuid "303d13d8-c568-5462-a96e-7d9428cc0d8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "303d13d8-c568-5462-a96e-7d9428cc0d8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463761} :answer-field/id #uuid "cabcaf59-25b4-5a2a-bea6-e13d0904de77" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $2$ along the path $y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464814} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f3edabc-c5eb-54d4-b7ff-8f9655427dfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463762} {:answer/id #uuid "f3850539-7158-5fcf-8ebd-98d1a0685dcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3850539-7158-5fcf-8ebd-98d1a0685dcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463763} :answer-field/id #uuid "34866a6a-1b03-5e91-a0b3-e6c757b74c41" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{3}$ along the path $y=x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464815} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28836dbd-a890-547c-9183-fb1de06ae39a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463764} {:answer/id #uuid "3afc1354-96f1-5aed-a802-292fe64f8795" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3afc1354-96f1-5aed-a802-292fe64f8795" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463765} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2aff006-d18e-573f-82f2-1f4b6cb7dfd9" :answer-field/key "The limit does not exist" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32eaab66-626d-536b-9465-8d972be98972" :question/math-academy-id "q-129405" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{2({0}^{2})-{0}^{2}}{{0}^{2}+2({0}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-0}{0+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $2$ along the path $y=0$” is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{0}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2({0}^{2})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{3}$ along the path $y=x$” is also true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}{3\\cancel{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit does not exist” is true. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29610715-333d-5e0c-9328-eec1d45f56ed" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Limits Along Different Paths for Multivariable Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048449 :topic/id #uuid "a05758d1-f2b4-5a86-b7b0-c2a4bb6dcb85" :topic/math-academy-id 1931 :topic/title "Limits and Continuity of Multivariable Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e982015-e57d-5a0b-a9cf-5d08deab7ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448356} {:answer/id #uuid "2459a454-5301-5e77-b21b-b6196bab14e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2459a454-5301-5e77-b21b-b6196bab14e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448357} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d95f94d-2076-5218-bb4b-c6ab553eb89a" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449218} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b6df36c-4778-5e0d-8a29-4c2efc4da127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448358} {:answer/id #uuid "51ef316d-e1c9-5b72-9ff3-7956a1c2c951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b6df36c-4778-5e0d-8a29-4c2efc4da127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448358} :answer-field/id #uuid "b396f2c8-dc63-5102-8ab9-0b273481f509" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $\\frac{2}{3}$ along the path $y=x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449219} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23411fdc-77e6-57da-b87b-f1f0a95f66cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448360} {:answer/id #uuid "ff37351c-4fe5-5bcc-ab1b-336319013805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff37351c-4fe5-5bcc-ab1b-336319013805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448361} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0e78afc-fd6f-5a29-a353-29016479df8c" :answer-field/key "The limit does not exist" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449220}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88abe9a3-7bd6-5ff9-8f3e-e809f8b5b178" :question/math-academy-id "q-129406" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2xy}{3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2xy}{3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{2(0)(0)}{3({0}^{2})-{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=0$” is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=0}\\,\\frac{2xy}{3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2x(0)}{3({0}^{2})-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $\\frac{2}{3}$ along the path $y=x$” is false. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{2xy}{3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x(x)}{3{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit does not exist” is true. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2xy}{3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048449 :topic/id #uuid "a05758d1-f2b4-5a86-b7b0-c2a4bb6dcb85" :topic/math-academy-id 1931 :topic/title "Limits and Continuity of Multivariable Functions"} :activity/title "Limits and Continuity of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571536} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572248}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29610715-333d-5e0c-9328-eec1d45f56ed" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Limits Along Different Paths for Multivariable Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048449 :topic/id #uuid "a05758d1-f2b4-5a86-b7b0-c2a4bb6dcb85" :topic/math-academy-id 1931 :topic/title "Limits and Continuity of Multivariable Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "810c6a8f-0958-52c6-b20f-d96a37359b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448362} {:answer/id #uuid "08cfa10d-b846-5e6d-bf35-9404324b2a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "810c6a8f-0958-52c6-b20f-d96a37359b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448362} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd5e3b0a-5393-557f-b53b-8a481a907ef0" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $4$ along the path $y={x}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449221} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88619661-430d-5de8-b84b-ec40f974019f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448364} {:answer/id #uuid "1a45e285-3045-5c04-8840-34af5a94d221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a45e285-3045-5c04-8840-34af5a94d221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448365} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cee3926-16f6-5e9e-9417-558226515e81" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449222} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e8e63f-6e04-57b4-8a7d-297ae9238284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448366} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec1f619-5c35-5d30-81b4-076f333cd284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ec1f619-5c35-5d30-81b4-076f333cd284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448367} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1158047-7645-528c-878f-9126eb72416b" :answer-field/key "The limit does not exist" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7bd92abc-0899-50b8-83be-62e32b920d95" :question/math-academy-id "q-129408" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{2({0}^{2})\\sqrt{0}}{{0}^{4}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $4$ along the path $y={x}^{4}$” is false. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{4}}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{4}}}{{x}^{4}+({x}^{4})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{8}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{4}}{{x}^{4}(1+{x}^{4})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2\\cancel{{x}^{4}}}{\\cancel{{x}^{4}}(1+{x}^{4})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2}{1+{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+{0}^{4}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $x=0$” is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,x=0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{y\\to 0}\\frac{2({0}^{2})\\sqrt{y}}{{0}^{4}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{y\\to 0}0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit does not exist” is true. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/id #uuid "be557898-2dc0-5c08-b4e7-63bbb4f08f56" :topic/math-academy-id 1198 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb45ac63-db12-5103-a680-0aca60a50ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448368} {:answer/id #uuid "a12d2978-9d54-59d4-9961-6bdc86f3c49f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb45ac63-db12-5103-a680-0aca60a50ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448368} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0935ce5-8cb9-5439-9df5-d68f6b26b1b4" :answer-field/key "The product $RS$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fb2ec2a-0f20-512b-93a8-4b9f3c962c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448370} {:answer/id #uuid "022054e0-5021-5992-9a69-680cffbd01c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fb2ec2a-0f20-512b-93a8-4b9f3c962c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448370} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2774138-c2fc-5876-84c5-93da8a175e9f" :answer-field/key "The product $RP$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449225} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb2b2b09-edcc-581e-920d-e47a8346fc6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448372} {:answer/id #uuid "c8393209-b177-529e-b28b-4beba3d7980d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8393209-b177-529e-b28b-4beba3d7980d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448373} :answer-field/id #uuid "887210a3-979a-5046-a639-10af689a9ba1" :answer-field/key "The product $SP$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449226}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22b7c2e7-9621-5013-a411-a722a7ceea01" :question/math-academy-id "q-129437" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $P$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix, $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, and $S$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $R$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{5\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $S$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $S$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe product $SP$ is well defined. The products $RS$ and $RP$ are undefined."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265765 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "624215ff-efdc-5b12-8d61-9d66371672d9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Valid Region to Define a Double Integral Over a Non-Rectangular Domain" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049229 :topic/id #uuid "e52ab899-5fcb-50d2-afee-4830a70f16df" :topic/math-academy-id 2616 :topic/title "Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "000fd319-21cd-5932-83a1-59aa9a87a731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463766} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9a3c6c-59a7-5af0-8a47-b00453e5ad3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "000fd319-21cd-5932-83a1-59aa9a87a731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463766} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcfd5bd0-78ee-5e58-a029-75f3bef6e4e0" :answer-field/key "$R=[-1,3]\\times [-2,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7581893-4afd-58a5-bc3f-c09a16f23deb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463768} {:answer/id #uuid "be899893-b4ad-50b0-8670-5d5bc7b0e630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7581893-4afd-58a5-bc3f-c09a16f23deb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463768} :answer-field/id #uuid "60c6461b-b5d1-5113-8d72-de726845724a" :answer-field/key "$R=[-1,2]\\times [-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464818} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76b528d7-b981-5937-928c-b87c5b84aa24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463770} {:answer/id #uuid "bedec7e3-9e92-5924-ab1e-9861d797ebf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bedec7e3-9e92-5924-ab1e-9861d797ebf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463771} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb7b5924-cef6-5250-b973-935f3b5e537c" :answer-field/key "$R=[-2,3]\\times [-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "16d77304-e003-57b3-942e-c991453c4142" :question/math-academy-id "q-129658" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b946843e712c6294e261cb3015b02bc065cd265763805cf046009a2db0d11b83.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangles $R=[-1,3]\\times [-2,1]$ and $R=[-1,2]\\times [-2,2]$ do not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangle $R=[-2,3]\\times [-2,2]$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $R=[-2,3]\\times [-2,2]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265767 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "624215ff-efdc-5b12-8d61-9d66371672d9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Valid Region to Define a Double Integral Over a Non-Rectangular Domain" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049229 :topic/id #uuid "e52ab899-5fcb-50d2-afee-4830a70f16df" :topic/math-academy-id 2616 :topic/title "Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55e2fcb9-82ec-576a-b76a-f1b11239f681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463772} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab6631b-6e22-5e28-9bcb-993e873e8d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ab6631b-6e22-5e28-9bcb-993e873e8d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463773} :answer-field/id #uuid "b758fd50-78d0-52d8-bbd1-86075774c6ba" :answer-field/key "$R=[-3,3]\\times [-1,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0c30927-e583-5ca9-a6f0-7e0b4a318bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463774} {:answer/id #uuid "3ccb29da-c9f3-577c-a679-15faf03f4314" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ccb29da-c9f3-577c-a679-15faf03f4314" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463775} :answer-field/id #uuid "7668413a-ca4c-5dea-916f-5271efb10fab" :answer-field/key "$R=[-4,4]\\times [-1,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5a466c9-0e63-51f9-a0a9-e948214d51e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463776} {:answer/id #uuid "14d3c007-3d62-5903-9565-26317d3effb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5a466c9-0e63-51f9-a0a9-e948214d51e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463776} :answer-field/id #uuid "81f86b98-4fb7-5b2e-a450-505398b9e9ef" :answer-field/key "$R=[-3,3]\\times [0,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60b29014-e789-5b3b-ac4b-a01d242582dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-129662" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+{y}^{2}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}9-{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}(9-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/4a/4a8671db243a19fb258f6144d6aba1b193e237ef93d45d877829f80b93bc7d36.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}9-{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(9-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangle $R=[-3,3]\\times [0,2]$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangles $R=[-3,3]\\times [-1,1]$ and $R=[-4,4]\\times [-1,1]$ cover the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $R=[-3,3]\\times [-1,1]$; $R=[-4,4]\\times [-1,1]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265769 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "624215ff-efdc-5b12-8d61-9d66371672d9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Valid Region to Define a Double Integral Over a Non-Rectangular Domain" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049229 :topic/id #uuid "e52ab899-5fcb-50d2-afee-4830a70f16df" :topic/math-academy-id 2616 :topic/title "Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answ