d}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & z \\\\ z & 1\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ z & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(3+z)-(2-{z}^{2})+5(-2-3z) \\\\  & =6+2z-2+{z}^{2}-10-15z \\\\  & ={z}^{2}-13z-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-48,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-13z-6 & =-48 \\\\ {z}^{2}-13z+42 & =0 \\\\ z & =\\frac{-(-13)\\pm \\sqrt{{13}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 42}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pm \\sqrt{1}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pm 1}{2} \\\\  & =6,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=6$ and $z=7.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048146 :topic/id #uuid "832923c0-f0e3-599f-af85-37cb7dae2658" :topic/math-academy-id 153 :topic/title "The Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbb6fbea-1024-5d3a-b73a-2652854807d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439539} {:answer/id #uuid "bd68a459-7909-5063-ad2f-80212bf601c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd68a459-7909-5063-ad2f-80212bf601c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439540} :answer-field/id #uuid "875c3194-24a6-51ec-b673-71d77e13cf9f" :answer-field/key "$x=-8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db104ef8-98d3-5cd8-a99b-bdad6e429a02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db