or the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 3 \\\\ 5 & x & 7 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =x|\\begin{aligned}x & 7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2x|\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}5 & x \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x(x-14)-2x(5-21)+3(10-3x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-14x+32x+30-9x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+9x+30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $22,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+9x+30 & =22 \\\\ {x}^{2}+9x+8 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{{9}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 8}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9\\pm 7}{2} \\\\  & =-8,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-8$ and $x=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a926134-0870-5528-985d-2c92e71158f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Linear ODEs" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050677 :topic/id #uuid "5e132315-9606-5b30-bee3-61f0209d40c4" :topic/math-academy-id 2548 :topic/title "Introduction to Second-Order Linear ODEs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86d0fa0c-d83e-5302-8b19-931a556d2598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463874} {:answer/id #uuid "5f240d2f-1e1c-5d49-baec-e89948422632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f240d2f-1e1c-5d49-baec-e89948422632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463875} :answer-field/id #uuid "79ca8d72-13b8-5039-a525-2d310ad8c033" :answer-field/key "$2{y}^{″}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}-y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464871} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f52e27e-69b6-5665-a21e-03f68b051fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463876} {:answer/id #uuid "a89b723d-942b-536a-99f1-180995a49f0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f52e27e-69b6-5665-a21e-03f68b051fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463876} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c322dd1-207e-5f01-a185-f2cc43f25df4" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+y{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464872} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3971c54-39c4-5514-becd-d741348b687e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463878} {:answer/id #uuid "2f404fad-6d9a-5bce-9290-c3cc1f239e76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f404fad-6d9a-5bce-9290-c3cc1f239e76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463879} :answer-field/id #uuid "f01fab60-26ab-58e5-a863-3b739a2c5149" :answer-field/key "$x{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "114cf182-dccf-5764-a411-6c6c3328247d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130670" :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}-y=1\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=2,b(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,c(x)=-1,$ and $f(x)=1.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{′}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\nx{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=x,b(x)=0,c(x)={x}^{2},$ and $f(x)={e}^{x}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $2{y}^{″}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}-y=1$; $x{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}$ only."}]
